Bringing Our Family and Church Youth Group to DEF CON

A Proposal for Learning, Service, and Christian Stewardship

⸻

Executive Summary

At first glance, DEF CON can sound intimidating. The name includes the word “hacker,” and many people associate hackers with crime or illegal activity. However, that stereotype only tells a small part of the story.

Today, cybersecurity professionals, software engineers, military personnel, law enforcement, educators, government agencies, hospitals, and major technology companies attend DEF CON every year. The conference is one of the world’s largest educational gatherings focused on understanding technology, protecting people, and improving computer security.

For a Christian family and youth group, DEF CON is not about learning how to break into systems.

It is about learning how to defend people, protect privacy, serve others, and wisely steward the technology God has allowed humanity to build.

⸻

Why Christians Should Care About Cybersecurity

Technology touches nearly every part of modern life.

* Churches use livestreams.
* Missionaries communicate online.
* Families bank online.
* Schools rely on computers.
* Hospitals store medical records.
* Ministries accept online donations.
