Attendees include:

* Students
* Families
* Teachers
* Professors
* Software developers
* Military personnel
* Government employees
* Cybersecurity companies
* Church technology volunteers
* Hobbyists
* Engineers

Thousands of people attend every year simply to learn.

⸻

Ethical Hacking

One of the biggest misunderstandings is the word “hacker.”

There are different kinds of hackers.

Black Hat

Uses skills illegally.

Steals information.

Damages systems.

Breaks laws.

⸻

White Hat

Uses permission.

Finds weaknesses.

Reports problems.

Improves security.

Protects organizations.

⸻

Gray Hat

Works somewhere in between.

May test systems without permission but often reports vulnerabilities rather than exploiting them.

⸻

Our goal would always be to learn White Hat security.

The goal is defense.

Not offense.

